-- StreetRise — Migration 044: MCAT (Manatee County) static GTFS
--
-- NOT APPLIED. Runbook: docs/apply-migrations-042-046.md.
-- Requires migration 042 (the tables).
--
-- 928 stops, 16 routes from Manatee County Area Transit's published bundle,
-- feed 20260814 (valid 2026-08-15 → 2027-06-04). Generated by
-- `scripts/build-transit-sql.ts`; DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
--
-- ── This one has no immediate effect, on purpose ────────────
-- StreetRise currently has ZERO public listings in Manatee County (checked
-- 2026-09-03: no active, map-ready rows anywhere in the Bradenton/Palmetto
-- bounding box). CLAUDE.md records migration 022 as having expanded into
-- "Manatee/Bradenton", but nothing from it is publicly visible today.
--
-- So this loads stops that nothing yet matches against. That is still worth
-- doing: it costs one table load, it means the first Manatee listing gets a
-- nearest-stop line the day it is added rather than months later, and — the
-- part that matters more — without it `src/lib/transit.ts` would read a
-- Bradenton address as "no coverage" and stay silent, which is correct but
-- indistinguishable from the county genuinely having no transit. It does.
--
-- ── Fares are NULL here, and that is deliberate ─────────────
-- MCAT ships `fare_attributes.txt` with a single $1.50 fare but NO
-- `fare_rules.txt`, so the feed provides no way to attach that price to a
-- route. It is very likely the flat fare for the whole system, but "very
-- likely" is not what this schema records. Every route lands with
-- fare_price NULL and is_fare_free FALSE — unknown, not free. If MCAT's
-- fares are wanted, they need reading off the agency's own fares page and
-- entering deliberately, not inferred from an unassignable row.
-- ================================================================


